    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Ncux17Yj6ANSAph5xngrN3)_\n\nA design record only (`adr/0020-tag-families.org`, status *proposed*, plus its row in `adr/README.org` and a CHANGELOG line). No code changes.\n\n**Decision proposed:** families of note tags are one alist, `sp-org-tag-families`, of `(FAMILY TAG…)` lists, which is the shape of Org's own `org-tag-groups-alist`. `org-tag-persistent-alist` (#105) is derived from it as Org group tags (`:startgrouptag` … `:endgrouptag`), so a tag search on a family finds its members. The record also lists the alternatives (raw group-tag syntax, plists, structs, nested names, vulpea properties, symbol plists), the consequences for `sp-org-tag-lint`, `sp-tag-emoji` and the prompts, and two open questions (family names, whether a tag in no family is refused).\n\n**Checked** (Emacs 29.3, headless): the family list converted to the group-tag form and `org-tag-alist-to-groups` returned the same families (a `(\"group\" . ?g)` member kept its key); in an Org buffer a `+music` match found a heading tagged `album`. **Not checked:** the converter and lookup functions (sketched in the record only), nested families, org-ql / vulpea behaviour with group tags, the completion grouping.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xrgdre7xkfaqJ3bbVqXTo5)_",
